<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n12523" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">dēcoctĭo</span></b> ,
			ōnis, f.
		decoquo (postclass.), <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a boiling down</i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> Prop. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>A.</b> Abstr.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">lentisci hoc modo,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cael.
						Aur. Tard. 2, 13, 165</span></i>
			.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>B.</b>
			Concret., <i>a decoction</i>,
				<i><span class="en">App. Herb. 77</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Cael.
				Aur. Acut. 3, 3, 17</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b>Trop.</b>, of an association, <i>a
				decoction, mixture</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">unius decoctioni universi respondere cogentur,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cod. Just. 11, 9, 5</span></i>
			; cf. <i><span class="en">Cod. Theod. 4, 9,
		3</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
